course: dictionary
lesson: 11310
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Yellow is the colour of the sun, bananas and lemons, but it can also mean a warning, or be a verb that means turning yellow. Read the words around it to find out which meaning is used.
explain: «The referee's word is final: a yellow card is a warning, a red card sends a player off.» Here yellow card is not about a colour. The clues are warning and sends a player off, so a yellow card is a warning to a player.
explain: «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower... and flies off with yellow balls of pollen packed on its back legs.» Here yellow describes the colour of the pollen. Always test your meaning: put it into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Yellow is a colour: the colour of the sun, bananas, lemons and egg yolks.
fact: Leaves or paper can yellow, which means they turn yellow with age.
fact: A «yellow card» in football is a warning to a player.
fact: A yellow traffic light means get ready to stop.
fact: In old slang, yellow means scared, but it is not a kind word to use.
exercise: «Faking a fall in football, called diving, is cheating and can earn a yellow card.» What does yellow card mean here? | A prize for the best player | A sign that the game is over | *A warning to a player | A colour for a football shirt
exercise: In «flies off with yellow balls of pollen», what does yellow describe? | The taste of the nectar | The sound the bee makes | *The colour of the pollen | The speed of the flight
exercise: «Leaves yellow with age.» In this sentence, what does yellow do? | *It means turn yellow in colour | It means fly away quickly | It means be very loud | It means be scared
test: «An emergency stop button... is usually red on a yellow background.» What colour is the background here? | Blue | Green | Red | *Yellow
test: In «Stars have different colours: our Sun is yellow-white», what does yellow-white describe? | A safety sign | A card | A warning | *A colour
exam: In «a yellow traffic light means get ready to stop», what kind of meaning does yellow have? | *A safety signal that means get ready | To turn yellow with age | A colour of the sun | Old slang for scared
